For TaptPay frontend work the user wants **simple, clean, minimalist, almost brutalist** UI: flat solid color blocks, white cards with hairline borders (`rgba(0,0,0,.08)`) and micro-shadows (`0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.06)`). **No glow, no glassmorphism, no big gradients, no blur.** They explicitly rejected a glassy/glowy landing page.

The reference design language is the **terminal** (`client/src/components/SmartTransitions.jsx`). Palette: navy `#040D6D`, sky-blue `#58ABFF`, off-white `#F4F4F4`, green `#1BBF85` (success), plus teal `#00DFC8`. Type: Outfit, oversized display weights, uppercase letter-spaced micro-labels, **lowercase button text** ("save", "launch", "get started").

Animations should be **seamless/smooth and best-in-class**: scroll-driven (pinned sections + reveal-on-scroll), framer-motion (`useScroll`/`useTransform`), Lenis smooth-scroll, count-ups, magnetic buttons, with `prefers-reduced-motion` fallbacks.

**Why:** The user values restraint + craft; "next level, best in the world" animation quality but within a minimalist visual frame.
**How to apply:** When building/editing TaptPay UI, mirror the terminal's flat aesthetic and palette; avoid glow/glass/gradient effects. The landing page (`client/src/pages/landing-page.tsx`) was rebuilt to this spec. Two key marketing messages: effortless instant payment collection (digital wallet/tap-to-pay) and rent collection for property management.
